export const BACKTEST: any = {"review":{"summary":"The ordinance likely conflicts with current state ADU law (Gov. Code §§ 66310-66342) in 16 places. Main problems: it cites repealed § 65852.2 and related sections, requires owner occupancy and deed restrictions for ADUs, uses the 2018 unpermitted-ADU date, caps multifamily detached ADUs at two, and sets impact-fee, parking, setback, architecture and historic standards that go beyond state limits. It also appears to omit the 15-business-day completeness determination and the appeal process (§ 66317(a)(2), (d)). Items not covered by loaded sources (septic percolation test E.6, shared-driveway rule F.6, ADU permit fee D.2.b) are unclear. This is a screening aid, not legal advice. Check the live code, since the city may have amended it.","issues":[{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(A) (also D.1.a.iv, E.5, E.8.a, G.2.a.ii): says the section is meant to comply with Gov. Code §§ 65852.2 and 65852.22 and cites § 65852.26.","conflict":"Those sections were renumbered by SB 477 and are no longer current law. The ordinance likely needs to cite and track §§ 66310-66342, including § 66342 for optional condominium conveyance.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, SB 477 / Gov. Code §§ 66310-66342","quote":"updated from 65852.2, 65852.22, 65852.23, and 65852.26 to Government Code sections 66310-66342"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(D.1.d): allows 'no more than two detached ADUs' on a lot with an existing or proposed multifamily dwelling.","conflict":"State law allows up to two on a proposed multifamily dwelling but up to eight on an existing one, not to exceed the number of existing units. The two-unit cap on existing multifamily lots likely conflicts.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66323(a)(4)(A)","quote":"up to eight detached ADUs are allowed on a lot with an existing multifamily dwelling, not to exceed the number of existing units on the lot"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(D.4.a.i): no impact fee only for an ADU 'less than 750 square feet in size'; also silent on JADUs.","conflict":"State law exempts ADUs of 750 square feet of interior livable space or less (and JADUs of 500 or less). The ordinance would allow fees on a unit of exactly 750 square feet and does not state the JADU exemption.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66311.5(c)","quote":"if it contains 750 square feet of interior livable space or less"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(D.4.a.ii): impact fees apply to an ADU 'that is 750 square feet or larger'.","conflict":"State law applies proportional fees only to ADUs larger than 750 square feet of interior livable space. Charging at exactly 750 square feet likely conflicts.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66311.5(c)","quote":"If an ADU contains greater than 750 square feet of interior livable space, impact fees shall be charged proportionately"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(E.7.b): ADUs permitted on or after Jan. 1, 2025 are subject to an owner-occupancy requirement.","conflict":"State law bars owner-occupancy requirements for ADUs, with a narrow exception for certain qualified-buyer sales under § 66341. The ordinance imposes it generally.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66315","quote":"instead mandates no owner-occupancy requirement for ADUs"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(E.7.c): all JADUs are subject to owner occupancy.","conflict":"State law requires owner occupancy only when the JADU shares sanitation facilities with the primary structure. JADUs with their own bathroom cannot be required to have it.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66333(b)","quote":"If the JADU does not have shared sanitation facilities, owner occupancy will not be required"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(E.8): requires a recorded deed restriction (no separate sale, size limits, enforcement, removal process) for every ADU and JADU before building permit issuance.","conflict":"The Handbook says a local agency cannot impose a deed restriction on an ADU. It allows a JADU deed restriction only for the no-separate-sale and size/attribute terms, so the added enforcement terms for JADUs may also go too far.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66315 (ADUs); § 66333(c) (JADUs)","quote":"A local agency cannot impose a deed restriction on an ADU."},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(F.2.a): one off-street parking space is required for each ADU.","conflict":"State law caps parking at one space per unit or per bedroom, whichever is less. A studio or efficiency unit with no bedroom likely cannot be required to provide a space.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66314(d)(10)(A)","quote":"Parking requirements for ADUs shall not exceed one parking space per unit or bedroom, whichever is less"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(F.2.b): replacement parking is not required only when a 'garage, carport, or other covered parking structure' is demolished or converted.","conflict":"State law also covers uncovered off-street spaces. Omitting them could be read to allow replacement requirements for uncovered spaces.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66314(d)(11)","quote":"may not require off-street parking spaces to be replaced when a garage, carport, covered parking structure, or uncovered parking space is demolished"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(F.2.c.v): the car-share parking exception applies only to a 'city-sanctioned, posted car-share pick-up or drop-off location' within one block.","conflict":"State law exempts the ADU whenever a car share vehicle is located within one block. The city's added 'sanctioned, posted' condition narrows the exemption.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66322(a)","quote":"When there is a car share vehicle located within one block of the ADU."},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(F.3.c): a detached ADU must be at least five feet from the primary building.","conflict":"State law says minimum separation requirements may not be applied if they unreasonably restrict ADUs unless required by the Building or Fire Code. The five-foot rule has no 800-square-foot safeguard like the one in F.4.c.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66314(d)(8)","quote":"Minimum distance or other requirements may not be applied if they would unreasonably restrict the creation of ADUs"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(F.3.d): no setback only if the ADU is in the same location and dimensions as an 'existing accessory building'.","conflict":"State law waives setbacks for ADUs created within an existing living area or accessory structure, or in a new structure in the same location and dimensions as any existing structure. The ordinance is narrower.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66314(d)(7)","quote":"No setback shall be required for an ADU or JADU created within an existing living area or accessory structure"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(F.7.a): exterior materials and colors must 'match the appearance and architectural design' of the primary dwelling.","conflict":"Matching appearance and design appears to call for personal judgment. The Handbook lists similar 'architecture style' language as subjective, and only objective standards may be applied to ADUs.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66313(i)","quote":"must maintain similar architecture style"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(F.8): an ADU on or within 600 feet of a California Register property must not be visible from any public right-of-way.","conflict":"State law allows standards that prevent adverse impacts on listed properties. A flat no-visibility rule that reaches neighboring lots likely goes beyond that and may unreasonably restrict ADUs.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66314(b)(1)","quote":"standards that prevent adverse impacts on any real property that is listed in the California Register of Historical Resources"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(G.2): protects unpermitted ADUs only if built before January 1, 2018, and cites § 65852.2.","conflict":"The cutoff is now January 1, 2020 under § 66311.7, so ADUs built in 2018-2019 are likely left unprotected. The repealed section is also cited.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66311.7(a)","quote":"Changes the date from January 1, 2018, to January 1, 2020"},{"rule":"§ 17.28.270(H): an ADU that does not meet the objective standards may be allowed through a discretionary Architectural Permit.","conflict":"State law requires a ministerial-only approval process for ADU applications. Sending applicants into a discretionary architectural review appears inconsistent, even if framed as optional.","citation":"state/hcd-adu-handbook.md, Gov. Code § 66315 / § 66317","quote":"Local agencies must provide an approval process that only includes ministerial provisions for the approval of ADU permit applications."}]},"grade":{"matches":[{"finding_number":1,"finding":"Cites deleted sections 65852.2/65852.22/65852.26","caught":true,"matched_issue":"§ 17.28.270(A) (also D.1.a.iv, E.5, E.8.a, G.2.a.ii): cites §§ 65852.2, 65852.22, 65852.26 which were renumbered; should cite 66310-66342"},{"finding_number":2,"finding":"One ADU + one JADU only; must allow any combination on single-family lot","caught":false,"matched_issue":""},{"finding_number":3,"finding":"Max 2 detached ADUs on multifamily lot; state allows up to 8","caught":true,"matched_issue":"§ 17.28.270(D.1.d): two detached ADU cap on existing multifamily lots conflicts with up to eight"},{"finding_number":4,"finding":"Detached ADU height capped at 16 ft","caught":false,"matched_issue":""},{"finding_number":5,"finding":"Owner occupancy required for ADUs after Jan 1, 2025","caught":true,"matched_issue":"§ 17.28.270(E.7.b): owner-occupancy requirement for ADUs permitted on or after Jan. 1, 2025"},{"finding_number":6,"finding":"Recorded deed restriction for ADUs and JADUs","caught":true,"matched_issue":"§ 17.28.270(E.8): requires recorded deed restriction for every ADU and JADU"},{"finding_number":7,"finding":"Car share parking exemption only if city-sanctioned, posted","caught":true,"matched_issue":"§ 17.28.270(F.2.c.v): car-share exception limited to 'city-sanctioned, posted' location"},{"finding_number":8,"finding":"Lot coverage etc. may limit ADU size below 800 sq ft","caught":false,"matched_issue":""},{"finding_number":9,"finding":"Materials, colors, windows must 'match' primary dwelling (subjective)","caught":true,"matched_issue":"§ 17.28.270(F.7.a): materials and colors must 'match the appearance and architectural design'; subjective"},{"finding_number":10,"finding":"Unpermitted-unit pathway only for units before 2018; must be 2020","caught":true,"matched_issue":"§ 17.28.270(G.2): protects unpermitted ADUs only if built before Jan 1, 2018; cutoff is 2020"}],"extra_issues":["§ 17.28.270(D.4.a.i): impact fee exemption only for ADU less than 750 sq ft; JADU exemption silent","§ 17.28.270(D.4.a.ii): impact fees apply at 750 sq ft or larger","§ 17.28.270(E.7.c): JADU owner occupancy for all JADUs","§ 17.28.270(F.2.a): one parking space per ADU regardless of bedrooms","§ 17.28.270(F.2.b): replacement parking exemption omits uncovered spaces","§ 17.28.270(F.3.c): five-foot separation from primary building","§ 17.28.270(F.3.d): no setback only for existing accessory building same location/dimensions","§ 17.28.270(F.8): California Register property 600 feet no-visibility rule","§ 17.28.270(H): discretionary Architectural Permit path"]},"input":"`san-clemente-muni-code-17-28-270.md` (full ordinance)"};
